<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns $300 mln in put options.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns $300 mln in put options.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico said on Monday it had placed all $300 million in dollar put options that it had offered for the month of April.</p>
<p>The options had an average premium of 21.86 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the put options was $1.77 billion.</p>
<p>The central bank said in a statement that 15 institutions placed bids, of which two were assigned the options.</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559))</p>
</text>
